# Question templates for the .tsv tables: relation => template | template, with {s} for the subject.
# Keep the held-out wordings in ../heldout.txt out of these templates, so the held-out score measures new phrasings.
chip => Which chip is in the {s}? | What chip does the {s} have? | What CPU does the {s} have? | What microcontroller is on the {s}? | {s} chip? | What is the processor of the {s}? | Tell me the chip of the {s}
clock => How fast is the {s}? | {s} clock speed? | At what speed does the {s} run? | What frequency does the {s} run at? | How many MHz is the {s}?
flash => How much flash has the {s}? | How much flash does the {s} have? | {s} flash? | How big is the program flash on the {s}? | How much flash memory is on the {s}?
ram => How much RAM has the {s}? | How much SRAM has the {s}? | {s} RAM? | What is the RAM of the {s}? | How much memory has the {s}?
psram => How much PSRAM has the {s}? | How much PSRAM does the {s} have? | {s} PSRAM? | What is the PSRAM of the {s}? | Does the {s} have PSRAM? | How big is the PSRAM on the {s}?
id => What is the board id of the {s}? | {s} board id? | Which juno.board value is the {s}? | What id does Juno use for the {s}? | How do I name the {s} in juno.board?
led => Which pin is the LED on the {s}? | Where is the built-in LED of the {s}? | {s} LED pin? | Which pin lights the {s} LED?
arena => How big is the arena on the {s}? | How big is the Juno arena on the {s}? | {s} arena? | How much arena does the {s} get?
wifi => Does the {s} have Wi-Fi? | Can the {s} connect to Wi-Fi? | {s} Wi-Fi? | Can the {s} join a network?
backend => Which backend does the {s} use? | What architecture is the {s}? | {s} backend? | Which Juno backend compiles for the {s}?
camera => Which camera has the {s}? | What camera does the {s} have? | {s} camera?
